/*  bracedK -- THE KANT BRACED BODY. SEQ 57 rung 4 / SEQ 63 part 2, 2026-08-13.
    FIRST LIVE FIRE OF parseRK, which has been BUILT-NEVER-FIRED since it was
    written.

    THIS FIXTURE IS incant/bindSeamB WITH THE KANT DOOR IN PLACE OF THE C++ ONE,
    and nothing else. Same field shape, same one bracket expression, same
    oracle. incant/bindSeamA is the interpreted oracle for both, and bindSeamB
    is the C++ arm this one is meant to match line for line -- which is what
    makes the two parseTrace outputs diffable, by design rather than by luck.

    THE BODY LIVES IN incant/parseCode, THE REAL ARTIFACT, reached through a
    FIXTURE-LOCAL fILEs entry. Nothing shared moves: promotion later is the one
    line below relocating into incant/setup, so the promotion diff is exactly
    the thing promoted. It also keeps the runtime-data bisect working on the
    shipping file, which is what made an earlier four-body bisect cost zero
    rebuilds.

    THE DOOR IS THE dlsym ONE -- parseMethod=parseViaKant, with parseTerms=3 so
    parseRuleMethod's refusal guard is live rather than warning. The MINT door
    stays unbuilt this rung; its index-guard parity item is the price of
    admission whenever it is next proposed.

    ⚠ THE SHIMS ARE REGISTERED HERE rather than in setup. A parse method whose
    body calls litK and parseRK needs those resolvable as commands at parse
    time. Keeping it local holds the eventual setup edit to the fILEs line
    alone. actK is deliberately NOT registered: this rung's body has no tail,
    because no kantDoor runs to clear the rule's method slot, so parse fires
    the action itself and a tail would fire it twice.

    ⚠ ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. The include and the bind both come BEFORE the
    define of fireIt, because an action body is parsed when it is DEFINED --
    so the fixture's own bracket expression parses through the kant door
    rather than through a hand-fed string.

    ⚠ 251 ALONE IS NOT A PASS. The interpreted arm has always produced 251, so
    a green value proves nothing about which arm answered. Read the arm by name
    in the trace: promote=0 is the generated arm and is what this rung claims,
    promote=1 means the bind did not take and the interpreted arm answered.
    That lesson was paid for at the IA-2 pin and applies here first.
*/
Start();
registry(cOMMANDs);
define litK immediateAction=litK; ;
registry(cOMMANDs);
define parseRK immediateAction=parseRK; ;
registry(cOMMANDs);
define traceParse immediateAction=traceParse; ;
traceParse();

registry(fILEs);
define parseCode File='incant/parseCode'; ;
include(parseCode);

define
    Braced parseTerms=3 parseMethod=parseViaKant;
    ;

register(BK);
define
    sumple width=1 height=2;
    fireIt code={
        sumple[width] = 251;
        print "  sumple width is now" sumple.width:;
        };
    ;
search reset stack Grokking BK list;
print "=== bracedK: kant Braced body, dlsym door, oracle 251 generated arm ===":;
fireIt();
print "BRACEDK SENTINEL":;
stop();
